{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784648155,"nonce":"70WhU/yCtCGdqZCh0FkZzJpL/ug=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\n(The report is terse; this maps the trailer-collection mechanism rather\nthan pinning a single defect line.)\n\n`b4 am` gathers review trailers by **git patch-id**, which is deliberately\nrevision-blind — an unchanged patch keeps the same patch-id across v1/v2/v3,\nso a Reviewed-by given on an older posting is carried onto the current one.\nThat carryover is by design. The \"confusing\" part is that it pools\nfollow-ups from *every* revision in the thread with no per-revision\nprovenance surfaced to the user.\n\n**Where the pooling happens** — `src/b4/__init__.py`:\n\n- `load_codereview_trailers()` (lines 320-344) builds one lore query,\n  `patchid:\u003cid\u003e OR patchid:\u003cid\u003e …`, over the patches of **all** series\n  versions, then extends `trailer_map[patch_id]` with every matching\n  message. Patches unchanged between revisions share a patch-id, so their\n  review messages from different revisions land in the same bucket.\n- The manual follow-up pass also crosses the revision boundary explicitly:\n  when a follow-up replies to a patch from an older revision\n  (`pmsg.revision != revision`), it is filed under that patch's patch-id for\n  carryover (`__init__.py:~451-456`).\n- Application is patch-id keyed only (`__init__.py:488`,\n  `for fmsg in self.trailer_map.get(lmsg.git_patch_id, ())`) — there is no\n  revision, thread-ancestry, or in-reply-to filter at this step.\n- `map_codereview_trailers()` emits the \"Analyzing N code-review messages\"\n  line (`__init__.py:6230`) — the count spans all revisions, which is itself\n  part of why the output reads as confusing (17 here).\n\n**Why it reads as \"picking up old trailers confusingly\":** the patch-id\nidentity is intentional, but (a) trailers earned on an older revision appear\non the new one with nothing in the output tying them to their origin\nrevision, and (b) this same collection feeds the mismatch accounting that\nmisfires in bug `e1ed6cb`. patch-id is computed from diff content only\n(`get_patch_id()`, `__init__.py:~2667`), so any patch whose diff is\nbyte-identical across revisions is indistinguishable here by construction.\n\nNote: the patch-id-only carryover is the exact-match behaviour by design;\nfuzzy subject/content matching lives behind `b4 trailers -u --fuzzy` and is\nintentionally not on this path.\n\n## Related bugs\n\n`e1ed6cb` (the mismatch-warning misfire fed by this same collection) and\n`116ac85` (trailer parsing) — all `trailers`-family. No fix suggestions per\nrequest.","files":null}]}